Algorithm: Threaded BST – Book ID Lookup System
1. Algorithm for Insertion of Book ID
Start.
Read the Book ID to be inserted.
Set ptr = root and parent = NULL.
Traverse the tree to find the correct position.
If the Book ID already exists, display a duplicate ID message and stop the insertion.
Create a new node with the given Book ID.
If the tree is empty, make the new node the root.
If the Book ID is smaller than the parent node, insert it as the left child and update the left thread.
Otherwise, insert it as the right child and update the right thread.
Display the successful insertion message.
Stop.
2. Algorithm to Find Inorder Successor
Start.
Read the Book ID.
Search for the Book ID in the tree.
If the Book ID is not found, display "Book ID not found." and stop.
If the right pointer is a thread, the right pointer is the inorder successor.
Otherwise, move to the right child.
Continue moving to the left child until the leftmost node is reached.
Display the inorder successor.
If no successor exists, display "No inorder successor (last book)."
Stop.
3. Main Algorithm
Start.
Create an object of the ThreadedBST class.
Display the menu:
Insert Book ID
Find Inorder Successor
Display Inorder Traversal
Display Threads
Exit
Read the user's choice.
Execute the corresponding operation.
Repeat Steps 3–5 until the user selects Exit.
Stop.
